Note : 
------
At the start of each simulation session, ensure that the file 
kmi_pl050/SourceMe is sourced to initialise certain environment variables.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Steps for running TicTalk VHDL simulations. 

Clock Enabled Tests - (Production)
------------------------------------------------
1. VHDL RTL simulations
------------------------

- Ensure that the Kmi_prod.tif has been copied to
  TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.tif
  (Note that the Kmi_prod.tif file would be generated from the BusTalk
  source file, Kmi_prod.c, residing in the BusTalk/bustests directory.)

- Additionally verify that a link exists from TicTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.tif
  to TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.tif. This link should have been created
  automatically by the build_Kmi script at the start of the setup process.

- In the TicTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL RTL
  uut         = $PERIPH/vhdl/uut/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the kmi_pl050/vhdl/uut directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the TicTalk/vhdl directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following files in the
   order given below:
   1. In the TicTalk/vhdl/sys    directory  : vcom rps.vhd
   2. In the TicTalk/vhdl/chip   directory  : vcom easy.vhd
   3. In the TicTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_tic.vhd)

- In the TicTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim tb_tic

2. VHDL NETLIST simulations
---------------------------

- Ensure that the Kmi_prod.tif has been copied to
  TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.tif
  (Note that the Kmi_prod.tif file would be generated from the BusTalk
  source file, Kmi_prod.c, residing in the BusTalk/bustests directory.)

- Additionally verify that a link exists from TicTalk/vhdl/tbench/infile.tif
  to TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.tif. This link should have been created
  automatically by the build_Kmi script at the start of the setup process.

- In the TicTalk/vhdl/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
  so that the library 'uut' points to the VHDL NETLIST
  uut         = $PERIPH/vhdl/uutNetlist/work

- Do a 'make clean' in the kmi_pl050/vhdl/uutNetlist directory

- Do a 'make clean' in the TicTalk/vhdl directory
  (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following files in the
   order given below:
   1. In the TicTalk/vhdl/sys    directory  : vcom rps.vhd
   2. In the TicTalk/vhdl/chip   directory  : vcom easy.vhd
   3. In the TicTalk/vhdl/tbench directory  : vcom tb_tic.vhd)

- In the TicTalk/vhdl/tbench directory, run simulations using
  vsim -sdfmax u_easy/u_rps/uKmi=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Kmi_Vhdl.sdf21
      tb_tic
  vsim -sdfmin u_easy/u_rps/uKmi=../../../vhdl/uutNetlist/Kmi_Vhdl.sdf21 
      tb_tic

